# Task completion – run build

When a coding task is finished (changes made, lints addressed, no follow-up edits pending), run the production build to confirm the project still compiles:

```bash
npm run build
```

- Run this **after** the task is complete, not during incremental edits.
- If the build fails, fix the reported errors before considering the task done.
- You may skip running the build if the user explicitly asks not to, or if the change was documentation-only and no code was modified.
